# Instagram feed (Instagram API with Instagram Login) — see docs/instagram-setup.md
# A long-lived Instagram user token (instagram_business_basic scope).
# Without it, the Instagram section falls back to static images.
#
# In production this is the seed token: the scheduled Netlify function
# (netlify/functions/refresh-instagram-token.mts) refreshes it weekly and
# stores the fresh value in Netlify Blobs, so it never expires.
IG_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Google Analytics 4 measurement ID (looks like G-XXXXXXXXXX).
# Set this in the Netlify environment (Site configuration → Environment
# variables), NOT here — it must be present at BUILD time because NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# vars are inlined into the client bundle, so a redeploy is required after
# changing it. When unset, GA is inert (layout.tsx renders nothing). Leave it
# unset locally so dev traffic isn't counted.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=
